      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-14 05:08:29",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "BREAKING: SpaceX says Boca Chica Beach will remain public, outlining major efforts to protect and restore it.\n\n• More than 50 tons of trash have been removed through weekly beach cleanups with the City of Starbase.\n\n• It has offered to invest tens of millions of dollars to fight beach erosion, restore the shoreline and preserve public access.\n\n• Its work with conservation partners has contributed to record sea turtle rescue efforts.\n\n• The proposed purchase covers approximately 1,200 acres surrounding the launch facility. Boca Chica Beach and the Texas coastline are excluded.\n\n• Around 600 acres would be permanently protected from development to preserve sensitive coastal habitat.\n\n• Proceeds from the proposed sale would help Texas invest in new parks and recreation in the Rio Grande Valley.\n\n• SpaceX is working with state agencies to improve safety around the launch facility while maintaining public beach access.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "cb_doge",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1498070100393754625/C2V-fbll_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-14 01:05:39",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-13T17:05:39.000Z",
        "id": "2121288392742982125",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXBUi_bbIAEcgbP.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 1125,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXBUi_bbIAEcgbP.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1125
          }
        ],
        "name": "DogeDesigner",
        "text": "BREAKING: SpaceX says Boca Chica Beach will remain public, outlining major efforts to protect and restore it.\n\n• More than 50 tons of trash have been removed through weekly beach cleanups with the City of Starbase.\n\n• It has offered to invest tens of millions of dollars to fight beach erosion, restore the shoreline and preserve public access.\n\n• Its work with conservation partners has contributed to record sea turtle rescue efforts.\n\n• The proposed purchase covers approximately 1,200 acres surrounding the launch facility. Boca Chica Beach and the Texas coastline are excluded.\n\n• Around 600 acres would be permanently protected from development to preserve sensitive coastal habitat.\n\n• Proceeds from the proposed sale would help Texas invest in new parks and recreation in the Rio Grande Valley.\n\n• SpaceX is working with state agencies to improve safety around the launch facility while maintaining public beach access.",
        "url": "https://x.com/cb_doge/status/2121288392742982125",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
